<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Banpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1858 CE (approx.) · capital Banpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bundela Rajput state of Bundelkhand whose Raja joined the revolt of 1857, leading to its confiscation by the British.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Banpur was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> principality in the hills south of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jhansi-state">Jhansi</a>, held by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> clan. The register dates it from around 1650, though its early history is not well documented.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its Rajas ruled a small upland territory with forts and agricultural villages. In the 1850s Raja Mardan Singh of Banpur joined the uprising of 1857 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, fighting alongside other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> chiefs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the revolt was suppressed in 1858, the British confiscated Banpur and added it to their own territory. Its lands now lie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitpur-district">Lalitpur district</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1650 CE – 1858 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:4.14%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1858 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Banpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mardan Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Banpur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1754&amp;focus=banpur-state" aria-label="Banpur State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7047 1313 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banpur State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7367 1569L7364 1601"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7367 1569h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7367 1569h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Banpur. <a href="/atlas?year=1754&amp;focus=banpur-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

